## Context

Ticket 1489 (closed, PR #2352) found these `/paper published` rows open for
the RDJHSS data paper (vol 10, pp 1-15, DOI 10.52024/fn48qf66) on host
doudou: 1 release subfolder has no `SHA256SUMS`; 3 the paper repo has no tag
and its STATE line no DOI; 5 the landing-page title drops "Multi-Source" and
shows no page range; 6 HAL's public record hal-05570600 is still the v2
preprint, v3 URL 404; 8 link check not run. The publisher's date is
2026-09-26, not 2026-11-09.

The author ruled on 2026-11-10 (decision A): a session on doudou finishes
the local rows and reads HAL, stopping before any outward act. `~/CNRS` has
no ticket store, so the harness carries this ticket; work inside the paper's
own repository goes through a session launched there, under its rules.

Allowed: local writes on doudou the open rows call for, the link check, a
read of HAL's public record. Not allowed, prepared and listed for the author
instead: any HAL deposit, PUT or SWORD call; `make sync` or any homepage
deploy; any push of commits or tags; any mail; any Zenodo or Zotero write.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each open row (1, 3, 5, 8) done, or carries a one-line reason
- [ ] HAL's public state recorded (version, DOI, last modification); whether
  the deposit sits in moderation is the author's to say, not inferred
- [ ] Each outward act listed here with its exact command and effect
- [ ] Before/after snapshots of papiers/sent, papiers/published, html,
  secretariat compared; only the entries the rows call for changed
